We are asked to compute the matrix product $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 4 & 8 \\ \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$.  Let this product be $\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}$. Then

\begin{align*} a &= (1)(5) + (2)(3) = 5 + 6 = 11 \\ b &= (4)(5) + (8)(3) = 20 + 24 = 44 \end{align*}
Thus, the result is $\begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 44 \end{pmatrix}$.

\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 44 \end{pmatrix}}

\boxed{11}

