Let $A = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 4 & 8 \end{pmatrix}$ and $B = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$.

We want to compute $A \cdot B = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 4 & 8 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$.

The product $A \cdot B$ is computed as follows:
\begin{align*} A \cdot B &= \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 4 & 8 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} (1 \cdot 5) + (2 \cdot 3) \\ (4 \cdot 5) + (8 \cdot 3) \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 5 + 6 \\ 20 + 24 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 44 \end{pmatrix} \end{align*} 

Thus, the answer is $\begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 44 \end{pmatrix}$.

\boxed{ \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 44 \end{pmatrix} }
